From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:36:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Oscillators: NEON interpolation weights and table reads,
 unswitched amplitude, NEON crude saw/square/triangle, exact VFP divisions,
 clz table number

Bit-exact: the same output, sample for sample, including what the vector loops write past the end.

- renderWave/renderPulseWave and the osc sync loops (vector_rendering_function.h, render_wave.h): the interpolation
  weights come from a vector of the next 4 phases, shifted left by tableSizeMagnitude (<= 13), instead of 4 scalar
  shifts and 4 vmov.16 per vector. Shifting left is exact modulo 2^32, so adding the shifted increments gives the same
  bits 16..31 as (phase >> (16 - tableSizeMagnitude)); vshrn #16 takes them. The table values are read with vld2.16
  per lane (value and next value into two vectors), the same two int16 the 32-bit lane loads read, which makes the
  vmovn/vshrn split unneeded; lane 0 with vld2 dup instead of the {0} inits. applyAmplitude is checked once, outside
  the loop (the same loop body twice).
- Crude saw and square below ~72 Hz, triangle below ~711 Hz (voice.cpp): 4 samples at a time after the numSamples & 3
  scalar ones; smmlar exactly as vmull_s32 + vrshrn_n_s64(#32) + vaddq_s32 (bits 32..63 of sum << 32 + a * b + 2^31,
  modulo 2^32); getTriangleSmall as min(phase, -phase) - 2^30 (unsigned), getSquare as INT32_MAX xor (phase >= pw).
  Phases and amplitudes step modulo 2^32 like the scalar adds; no new signed arithmetic.
- Osc sync and PW (render_wave.h, voice.cpp): the 32-bit divisions by vdiv.f64 (asm, correctly rounded; truncated it is
  the integer quotient for 32-bit operands), the two 64-bit analog square PW divisions by vdiv.f64 plus a remainder
  correction (the double quotient is q or rounds up to q + 1); the rare cases (resetter phase in the next cycle, zero
  divisor) keep the 64-bit division.
- getTableNumber: clz picks the first table of the octave, at most 2 comparisons follow (identical to the old one for
  all 2^32 inputs).

Bench (ARM, tests/bench/oscillators): 17 fixed cases + 30000 randomized ones identical, 28-64% fewer instructions.
Song (demand, per 128 samples): 1,370,014 -> 1,292,117 (renderOsc 279,575 -> 201,681); all 650,108 renderOsc calls
identical by value (song_trace.sh).

